<section id="guarantees" class="guar-sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kick">Guarantees</p>
    <h2>Built so it never makes things <em>worse</em>.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Product rules, not marketing. If it doesn’t pay off, it turns itself off.</p>
    <div class="guar4" data-reveal>
      <div class="g4"><span class="gi">01</span><b>Your main session is never routed.</b><p>Opus keeps planning. Only the subagents it delegates to go through Horsy.</p></div>
      <div class="g4"><span class="gi">02</span><b>It never blocks you.</b><p>If Horsy fails or is slow, everything runs as before. Checks have a retry cap, and <code>/horsy off</code> always gets you out.</p></div>
      <div class="g4"><span class="gi">03</span><b>It turns itself off where it loses.</b><p>The engine only routes a task type down when expected cost and time, retries included, come out lower. Losing types go back to your default.</p></div>
      <div class="g4"><span class="gi">04</span><b>Honest receipts.</b><p>Net time, net cost, errors caught. Even when the number is negative.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
